COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Adult Basic-Study Skills</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="77" RECORDID="6100"><COL><DATA>ABE 0710</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This is an introductory course examining the basic skills. It consists of a review of reading, math, English, science, and social studies. The course may serve as a pre-GED course for those students working toward a GED goal.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Adult Basic Education I</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>4</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>4</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="78" RECORDID="6101"><COL><DATA>ABE 0711</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Reading Readiness concentrates on basic concepts, letter identification, describing, listening and comprehension, phonics, phonemes, syllabication, rhyming, context clues, and main idea.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Reading Readiness</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="75" RECORDID="6102"><COL><DATA>ABE 0712</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This course focuses on math readiness. It covers number recognition, cardinality, ordinality, sets, matching, association, conservation, measurements, problem solving, place value, and money.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Math Readiness</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="82" RECORDID="6103"><COL><DATA>ABE 0713</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Adult Basic Education II is a continuation of ABE 0710, concentrating on a review of reading, math, English, science, and social studies. This course may serve as a pre-GED course for those students working towards a GED goal. PREREQUISITE: ABE 0710 Adult Basic Education I or consent of instructor.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Adult Basic Education II</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>4</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>4</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="76" RECORDID="6104"><COL><DATA>ABE 0714</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This course is designed for those individuals who wish to improve their basic reading skills. The course is designed for students reading between fourth and eighth grade level. Development of vocabulary, fluency, alphabetics, and comprehension are emphasized. It is designed for evidence based reading strategies and instruction.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Basic Developmental Reading</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="75" RECORDID="6107"><COL><DATA>ABE 0724</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This course is a basic study of government and law. It focuses on how the structure of government and the functions of the legal system delineate rights and obligations of citizens. Topics include the Constitution, the three branches of the Federal Government, individual influences on government, and state and local government.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Government and Law I</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>3</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>3</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="77" RECORDID="6108"><COL><DATA>ABE 0725</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This is the second in the sequence of basic study of government and law. It focuses on how the structure of government and the functions of the legal system delineate rights and obligations of individuals. Topics include legal documents, the courts and judicial system, an individual&apos;s rights, and obligations and government services. PREREQUISITE: ABE 0724 Government and Law I or consent of instructor.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Government and Law II</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>3</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>3</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="78" RECORDID="6109"><COL><DATA>ABE 0726</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This is an introductory course designed to develop basic reading and language skills. Major focus is on grammar, spelling, sentence construction, paragraph construction and essay writing.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Pre-GED Skills:  English</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="76" RECORDID="6110"><COL><DATA>ABE 0727</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This is an introductory course designed to develop basic skills in mathematics. Focus is on a review of whole numbers, fractions, decimals, percents, calculator skills, graphs, charts, geometry measurements, statistics, probability, and basic concepts of algebra.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Pre-GED Skills:  Math</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="75" RECORDID="6111"><COL><DATA>ABE 0728</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This course is an introductory survey course in history, world history, geography, economics, civics, government, and other areas of social studies. Topics include major events in American and world history, basic principles of economics, civics, government, and the United States Constitution.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Pre-GED Skills:  Social Studies</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW><ROW MODID="80" RECORDID="6112"><COL><DATA>ABE 0729</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>This introductory survey course is designed to develop knowledge and skills in the area of physical, life, earth, and space science. The course deals with basic concepts in botany, zoology, and physical science.</DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA></DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>X</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Pre-GED Skills:  Science</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Y</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>0</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>2</DATA></COL><COL><DATA>Lecture. Variable. Repeatable 3 times.</DATA></COL></ROW></RESULTSET></FMPXMLRESULT>